# picoclaw — example environment file
#
# Copy to `.env` for local development:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored. `.env.example` is committed and contains
# **placeholders only** — never paste real tokens, keys, or secrets here.
# See docs/DECISIONS.md D012 for the full secrets policy.
#
# In production use systemd `EnvironmentFile=` or launchd
# `EnvironmentVariables` instead of a .env file.
#
# Variables are grouped by the milestone that introduces them. Anything
# beyond M0 is commented out — uncomment as you reach the corresponding
# milestone (see ROADMAP.md).


# =============================================================================
# M0 — Skeleton (active now)
# =============================================================================

# Runtime data directory. Holds store.sqlite, ipc/, sessions/, wrappers/.
# Default: ./data (resolved to absolute path at startup).
PICOCLAW_DATA_DIR=./data

# slog level: debug | info | warn | error
PICOCLAW_LOG_LEVEL=info

# slog format: text | json
PICOCLAW_LOG_FORMAT=text

# Telegram chat ID of the owner. The owner chat has elevated privileges
# (register chats, schedule for others, RW access to the store, full
# secret allowlist). Optional in M0; required from M2 onward.
# PICOCLAW_OWNER_CHAT_ID=123456789


# =============================================================================
# M1 — Telegram echo
# =============================================================================

# Bot token from @BotFather. Required from M1 onward.
# Privacy mode: disable in BotFather (/setprivacy → Disable) and re-add
# the bot to every existing group — see docs/HANDOFF.md.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=


# =============================================================================
# M2 — Direct API agent
# =============================================================================

# Anthropic API key for the direct-API agent path.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=


# =============================================================================
# M3.6 — Observability (D014)
# =============================================================================
# Both subsystems are off by default. Set the addr/endpoint to enable.

# Prometheus pull endpoint. Empty (default) = no listener at all.
# PICOCLAW_METRICS_ADDR=127.0.0.1:9090
# PICOCLAW_METRICS_PATH=/metrics
# PICOCLAW_METRICS_DROP_CHAT_LABEL=0

# OpenTelemetry OTLP traces. Empty (default) = no-op tracer provider.
# PICOCLAW_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:4317
# PICOCLAW_OTLP_PROTOCOL=grpc            # grpc | http (auto from URL scheme if empty)
# PICOCLAW_OTLP_INSECURE=0               # 1 to skip TLS verify (local collector only)
# PICOCLAW_TRACE_SAMPLE_RATE=1.0
# PICOCLAW_SERVICE_NAME=picoclaw
# PICOCLAW_SERVICE_VERSION=

# OTLP headers may carry vendor API keys. SECRET MATERIAL — placeholder only.
# Comma-separated key=value pairs. Logged with redaction (D012).
# PICOCLAW_OTLP_HEADERS=x-honeycomb-team=REPLACE_ME


# =============================================================================
# M5 — Container runtime (D003, D013) — ACTIVE FROM M5
# =============================================================================

# Set to 1 to skip the runner/Docker subsystem entirely (the binary
# still opens the store and runs the telegram echo). The subprocess
# fallback that actually runs `claude` on the host is not yet wired —
# this is a kill switch, not yet a working alternative mode.
# PICOCLAW_NO_CONTAINER=0

# Container image picoclaw spawns per chat. Build it with:
#   docker build -t picoclaw-agent:latest container/
# PICOCLAW_CONTAINER_IMAGE=picoclaw-agent:latest

# Per-chat resource caps. Not yet consumed (M6 wires them into
# BuildContainerArgs).
# PICOCLAW_CONTAINER_MEM=4g
# PICOCLAW_CONTAINER_CPUS=2
# PICOCLAW_CONTAINER_PIDS=1024

# Idle-kill timeout. Not yet consumed (M6 wires the idle watcher).
# PICOCLAW_IDLE_TIMEOUT=30m

# Boot-time leftover-container cleanup.
# Running containers at the current build version are kept across a
# picoclaw restart; everything else is stopped and removed. Set the
# var to any truthy value to disable the cleanup pass (debug only).
# PICOCLAW_LEFTOVER_CLEANUP_DISABLED=

# picoclaw checkout root. Defaults to os.Getwd() at startup, which is
# the right answer when running `go run ./cmd/picoclaw` from the
# project directory. Set explicitly when running the built binary
# from somewhere else.
# PICOCLAW_REPO_ROOT=

# Mount allowlist file (operator-managed, chmod 0600). Missing file
# is not an error — picoclaw runs with only the standard per-chat
# mounts. Default: ${PICOCLAW_DATA_DIR}/mount-allowlist.json
# PICOCLAW_MOUNT_ALLOWLIST=


# =============================================================================
# M9 — Native memory (D016)
# =============================================================================

# Embedding provider: openai | voyage | ollama
# PICOCLAW_EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=openai
# PICOCLAW_EMBEDDING_MODEL=text-embedding-3-small
# PICOCLAW_EMBEDDING_DIM=1024            # frozen after first run

# Provider API keys (memory layer + I3 voice transcription).
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# VOYAGE_API_KEY=
